# A developer's own memkit config, which belongs in ~/.cache/memory-recall/ and
# never in a clone. Nothing here reads it — the wrappers admit a config only
# from the install option or the harness's data dir — but a payload file named
# like a config is a thing the next reader will wire back up, and
# test_the_payload_root_carries_no_config_of_its_own is the assertion that
# stops it. This line stops the accidental `git add -A` that would get there
# first.
/memkit.json
